# Agent workflow (Cursor)

The main Agent is the orchestrator. Specialist roles live in `.cursor/agents/` and are invoked
as subagents. Shared project knowledge is in `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/skills/`.

## Flow

`architect` → `<owner_role>` (editor-dev | codegen-dev | server-dev | copilot-dev) → `verifier`
→ optional `manim-reviewer` / `ui-reviewer` → `docs-keeper`.

The contract between roles is `docs/handoffs/<yyyy-mm-dd>-<slug>.md`, created from
`docs/handoffs/TEMPLATE.md`. Each role appends only its own section. Frontmatter `status`,
`owner_role`, `next_tool` is the only place task status lives. Handoff files are committed.

## When to delegate

- Non-trivial request (touches more than one layer, changes persisted schema, changes emitted
  Python, adds an endpoint, or is an `idea.md` item): start with `architect`, then follow the
  handoff. Do not implement before a plan exists.
- Small fix inside one file with an obvious test: do it directly, then still run `verifier`.
- Any change under `manim-timeline/src/codegen` or `src/lib/time.ts`: `codegen-dev` only.
- Any change to `measure_server.py` / `hebrew_*.py`: `server-dev` only.
- Any change under `manim-timeline/src/agent`: `copilot-dev` only.
- After an implementer reports done: always `verifier` before telling the user it is done.
- Generated Python changed shape, or a visual defect is reported: `manim-reviewer` in the
  background while other work continues.
- New or changed panel/timeline UI: `ui-reviewer` in parallel with `verifier`.
- `status: docs`: `docs-keeper`.

## Handoff from / to OpenCode

If a handoff's `next_tool` is `opencode`, do not pick it up unless the user says so. When passing
work to OpenCode use `/handoff-opencode`, which records a dated note, sets `next_tool: opencode`,
runs the quick gates, and commits `Checkpoint: <slug> — <status> (→ opencode)`.

## Guard rails (also in AGENTS.md)

Run `git status` first; uncommitted files you did not create are WIP — leave them. `npm` only
from `manim-timeline/`; `pytest`/`uvicorn` only from the repo root. Never read `assets/audio/`,
`media/`, `render_debug/`, or the sidecar `.exe`. No `git push`, hard resets, or branch deletes
without explicit instruction.
